 "post": {
  "title": "He Paid $50. Now He Wants $200 #shorts",
  "description": "Dev won't sell his old armchair for less than four times what he paid. Psychologists call it the endowment effect: owning something makes it feel more valuable. In Kahneman, Knetsch & Thaler's 1990 mug experiments, students given a coffee mug wouldn't sell it for less than about $7 (median $7.12), while buyers would pay only about $3 (median $2.87). The fix: ask 'would I buy this today at this price?' #psychology #shorts #money",
